  "status": "private-preflight-not-public-evidence",
  "notes": "This contract pins the bounded IEEE 1516.2-2025 Clause 3.3.1 name-convention preflight. Umbra applies XML NCName character rules, reserves periods for directed-interaction qualified class paths, rejects unknown user-defined HLA-prefixed names after MIM names are known, and rejects the NA marker for named table entries. The supplied Restaurant enumerator named NA remains accepted as an explicit source-compatibility exception because the official example conflicts with the prose; that tension is logged in the Requirements-Lab observation ledger. Individual DIF validation remains owned by the vendored schema, and this is private composition traceability only, not a FOM conformance or public-service evidence claim.",
